@startuml j9-shared-tickets
!include style.iuml
title J9 Tickets shared between visitors: the store order
actor "Patient\n(one device)" as Patient
participant "POST /api/chat" as Api
participant "db.ts\n(storeMode)" as Db
database "Postgres (Neon)\nused when its address is set" as PG
database "Redis of the host\nlive store today" as KV
database "Server memory" as Mem
participant "/api/tickets" as T
actor "Staff\n(another device)" as Staff
participant "GET /api/health" as H
autonumber

Patient -> Api : a message that needs a person
Api -> Db : insertTicket(...)
alt DATABASE_URL is set (not so on the live site)
  Db -> PG : INSERT INTO tickets
else the Redis address and token are set (the live site)
  Db -> KV : HSET <prefix>tickets, over REST, 6 second limit
  note right of KV : keys under one prefix: clinic, tickets, msgs:<chat id>
else neither is set
  Db -> Mem : kept in this server instance only
end
alt the store cannot be reached
  Db --> Api : the fault is noted (stored: false), never thrown
  Api --> Patient : the reply, plus "please call the clinic" when a ticket was lost
else stored
  Api --> Patient : the reply
end

Staff -> T : GET /api/tickets
T -> Db : listTickets()
T --> Staff : the same tickets, without chat ids; 503 when the store cannot be read

H -> Db : healthCheck()
note right of H
ok and the store name (neon, kv or memory), and whether
an AI key is set, never the key. Memory on the host is
a fault: not ok, status 503. The live site says kv.
end note
@enduml
